% Transcutaneous Electrical Joint Stimulation Devices (TEJSD): LCD L34821
% and its Policy Article A52713 (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS
% model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category,
% continued need, refills) and decides the claims for a TEJSD (E0762) and
% the replacement wrap or strap that positions its electrodes (A4465) — by
% concluding NOTHING about their medical necessity. The LCD states no
% coverage criterion; it states a non-coverage: "There is insufficient
% published clinical evidence to establish that treatment with
% Transcutaneous Electrical Joint Stimulation Devices (TEJSD) (HCPCS code
% E0762) meets the requirements to be considered reasonable and necessary
% for the treatment of osteoarthritis or any other condition. Claims for
% TEJSD (code E0762) will be denied as not reasonable and necessary." The
% supplies follow the device: "Since code E0762 is not considered to be
% reasonable and necessary (see above), claims for codes A4465, A4495,
% A4557, and A4595 to be used with code E0762 will be denied as not
% reasonable and necessary."
%
% How this is read. The device is within the durable medical equipment
% benefit (Policy Article A52713: "A Transcutaneous Electrical Joint
% Stimulation Device (TEJSD) is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment
% benefit"), so a claim for it passes applicability when the record shows a
% home — the article's own exclusion, "Provision of TEJSD to beneficiaries
% in a Place of Service or facility considered to be other than home will be
% denied as statutorily non-covered", is the home condition of dmepos.le —
% and is not reasonable and necessary, no rule concluding that a claim for
% E0762 is. (The stage query names the remedy for such a claim, not the
% question: it blames the earliest section holding a rule the attempt tried,
% and the question section here holds none.) Of the supply codes the LCD names, only A4465
% is the TEJSD's own ("Code A4465 is used for replacement only of any
% wrap/strap used to position and hold electrodes used with TEJSD in
% place"); A4557 and A4595 are the TENS supply codes decided by tens.le,
% and A4495 (a wrap for a TENS) is not decided here. The combination with a
% brace ("When TEJSD is used concurrently or in combination with any type of
% brace, there no reimbursement possible for the TEJSD device") and the
% conductive garment E0731 used with it add nothing to a device no rule
% covers, and are not modelled; the PDAC coding verification is coding, not
% coverage.
%
% The Medicare Appeals Council decided the claims of this kind before the
% LCD (BioniCare Medical Technologies, 2009; International Rehabilitative
% Sciences): the BIO-1000, billed under E0762 for osteoarthritis of the
% knee, "is not a TENS unit" and was not shown to be reasonable and
% necessary. tejsd_cases.le runs one of them.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base tejsd includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base tejsd includes:

LCD L34821 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=34821".
the text of LCD L34821 is at "sources/lcd/L34821.txt".
Policy Article A52713 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52713".
the text of Policy Article A52713 is at "sources/article/A52713.txt".

section applicability is:

tejsd has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the device and its own replacement wrap.
rule tejsd_codes with provenance Policy Article A52713,
        confer "A transcutaneous electrical joint stimulation device (TEJSD) coded (E0762) is a noninvasive device that delivers electrical stimulation intended to reduce the level of pain and symptoms associated with arthritis in a joint":
the policy for code a code is tejsd
    if the code is in ["E0762", "A4465"].

% Their benefit: durable medical equipment — used in the home, or nothing
% ("Provision of TEJSD to beneficiaries in a Place of Service or facility
% considered to be other than home will be denied as statutorily
% non-covered": the home condition of dmepos.le).
rule tejsd_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52713,
        confer "A Transcutaneous Electrical Joint Stimulation Device (TEJSD) is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is tejsd.

section question is:

% No rule concludes that a claim for E0762 or A4465 is reasonable and
% necessary: "There is insufficient published clinical evidence to establish
% that treatment with Transcutaneous Electrical Joint Stimulation Devices
% (TEJSD) (HCPCS code E0762) meets the requirements to be considered
% reasonable and necessary for the treatment of osteoarthritis or any other
% condition. Claims for TEJSD (code E0762) will be denied as not reasonable
% and necessary." (LCD L34821), and for the wrap: "claims for codes A4465,
% A4495, A4557, and A4595 to be used with code E0762 will be denied as not
% reasonable and necessary."
